WEBVTT

00:02.920 --> 00:04.650
Uh...

00:05.390 --> 00:08.400
I can't see the TV, Umi.

00:08.720 --> 00:11.870
Just look over my shoulder.

00:11.870 --> 00:14.370
I dunno about this setup, though.

00:14.370 --> 00:16.970
It's making me feel kinda awkward.

00:17.290 --> 00:21.260
Hey, it's just the two of us right now.

00:21.960 --> 00:25.510
Better be careful not to go any higher.

00:27.350 --> 00:28.840
Maki, you perv.

00:29.350 --> 00:31.260
I haven't done anything yet.

00:31.260 --> 00:37.850
I'm just prepping for the scenario where 
you end up touching my chest somehow.

00:37.850 --> 00:39.690
A pre-perv, if you will.

00:39.980 --> 00:41.830
Please don't.

00:43.890 --> 00:46.940
All right, time's up! We win!

00:46.940 --> 00:49.570
We're back in our rightful place 
atop the leaderboard!

00:49.570 --> 00:53.990
Yeah. Looks like this setup 
might actually work out.

00:53.990 --> 00:57.450
See? You thought so too, right?

00:57.700 --> 01:04.620
When you hold me, I feel like I can take 
more risks because you've got my back.

01:04.620 --> 01:07.380
She has no clue how hard it is for me.

01:07.740 --> 01:09.590
Her sweet scent in the air,

01:09.590 --> 01:12.680
the soft touch of her body...

01:12.680 --> 01:16.640
Okay, let's try another round like this!

01:16.980 --> 01:18.430
Our time's almost up.

01:18.430 --> 01:20.350
Enough gaming. Get ready to go.

01:20.670 --> 01:24.560
What?! I was just getting into the groove.

01:24.920 --> 01:26.570
Quit whining.

01:26.570 --> 01:29.280
You know you need to stick to the curfew 
you and Sora-san agreed on.

01:29.280 --> 01:30.570
Grr...

01:31.790 --> 01:33.990
Uh... nope.

01:34.330 --> 01:36.200
I haven't said anything.

01:36.200 --> 01:38.830
You don't want to leave, right?

01:39.230 --> 01:41.410
That's why I give you a pre-nope.

01:41.410 --> 01:44.130
Don't copy me, you jerk!

01:47.140 --> 01:48.210
Hey...

01:49.060 --> 01:51.360
It's almost Valentine's Day.

01:52.060 --> 01:54.430
Oh, right, it is that time of year.

01:54.430 --> 01:59.140
I'll put my heart into 
making chocolate for you.

01:59.140 --> 02:00.950
O-Okay.

02:01.760 --> 02:06.350
I never thought Valentine's Day 
would ever be a thing on my calendar.

02:06.980 --> 02:08.320
I see.

02:08.320 --> 02:11.760
It's a lot more exciting 
when you're dating someone, huh?

03:43.830 --> 03:44.700
Here.

03:45.190 --> 03:46.210
Thank you.

03:49.710 --> 03:51.460
Here, class rep.

03:52.270 --> 03:56.170
Thanks. You're handing 'em out 
to everyone in class?

03:56.490 --> 04:01.850
We've spent close to a year together, 
so it's the least I can do.

04:01.850 --> 04:04.890
Oh, feel free to pull out the stops 
with the return gift.

04:04.890 --> 04:06.660
Show me the money.

04:07.420 --> 04:10.920
One pack of bulk-bought 
biscuits for her, then.

04:13.120 --> 04:17.570
Umi and I are making chocolate 
tomorrow with Ninacchi.

04:17.570 --> 04:19.410
Look forward to it.

04:19.410 --> 04:22.460
It's your first Valentine's Day 
with Maki-kun.

04:22.460 --> 04:25.560
You want to give him something 
that tastes nice, don't you?

04:25.560 --> 04:27.870
Yeah, is that a problem?

04:27.870 --> 04:30.260
Not at all.

04:30.260 --> 04:33.220
If anything, you're being 
super cute right now.

04:33.220 --> 04:35.720
You agree, right, Maki-kun?

04:35.720 --> 04:37.670
Sure, I guess.

04:44.740 --> 04:46.120
'Sup.

04:46.120 --> 04:48.180
Happy Valentine's!

04:48.640 --> 04:52.400
As promised, the chocolate 
the three of us made!

04:52.400 --> 04:53.880
Thanks.

04:54.860 --> 04:56.600
So...

04:56.600 --> 05:00.800
Oh, the plan was for Umi to come with us.

05:00.800 --> 05:04.010
But she's not satisfied with 
the chocolate she's made for you,

05:04.010 --> 05:06.200
so she stayed behind.

05:06.500 --> 05:10.550
She probably took the stuff 
back home and is trying again.

05:10.550 --> 05:11.910
I see.

05:14.900 --> 05:18.530
Whew, that hits the spot.

05:16.800 --> 05:19.380
AMAMI-SAN AND NITTA-SAN TOLD ME WHAT'S
GOING ON. EVERYTHING OKAY OVER THERE?

05:16.800 --> 05:19.380
JUST CHILL WITH THEM FOR A BIT

I'LL BE THERE IN NO TIME

05:18.300 --> 05:19.380
GOT IT. I'LL BE WAITING

05:20.640 --> 05:22.340
Give her a call.

05:22.620 --> 05:25.460
You're worried about Asanagi, right?

05:25.460 --> 05:27.310
Just tell her that, then.

05:27.310 --> 05:30.510
I think that's a good idea, too.

05:30.510 --> 05:34.690
Umi seemed to be struggling 
because it wasn't going too well.

05:34.690 --> 05:35.390
Okay.

05:42.840 --> 05:45.140
What's up, Maki?

05:45.140 --> 05:48.800
What, did you get worried 
because I haven't shown up?

05:48.800 --> 05:50.790
Kinda, yeah.

05:50.790 --> 05:54.150
I had a little trouble, 
but I'll be done soon.

05:54.150 --> 05:57.090
I'll bring it over in a little bit.

05:57.090 --> 06:00.530
I see. That's good to hear.

06:01.270 --> 06:03.220
Hey, Umi?

06:03.220 --> 06:04.760
What?

06:05.600 --> 06:09.670
Yeah, she's in full bullheaded mode.

06:11.430 --> 06:13.200
What is it, Maki?

06:15.910 --> 06:18.020
Can I come over now?

06:24.140 --> 06:25.770
Umi, uh...

06:25.770 --> 06:26.570
Sorry.

06:26.860 --> 06:31.540
I wasn't planning to go 
so tryhard at first,

06:31.860 --> 06:35.180
but once I got started, 
I just couldn't back down.

06:35.750 --> 06:39.000
Do you mind if I ask what you're making?

06:39.630 --> 06:42.970
Gâteau chocolate, for what it's worth.

06:43.660 --> 06:47.540
That's hard to make even for me, 
and I make sweets quite often.

06:48.090 --> 06:51.620
Umi's not much of a cook, 
so it may be a tall order for her.

06:53.150 --> 06:57.250
I'm being really 
out-of-character now, aren't I?

06:58.410 --> 07:00.260
Yeah, you are.

07:01.270 --> 07:02.570
Right?

07:02.570 --> 07:05.340
I knew that Yuu and Nina were at a loss,

07:05.340 --> 07:07.680
but I still got all obsessive.

07:08.070 --> 07:11.150
I'll stop once I finish 
the one I'm making right now.

07:11.150 --> 07:13.200
Will you please try it for me?

07:13.200 --> 07:17.680
I don't mind, but will you 
really be satisfied with that?

07:18.310 --> 07:19.170
Yeah.

07:19.170 --> 07:25.380
I was wrong to try to get it 
perfect on my first try.

07:25.670 --> 07:30.040
I get that it's important to make 
compromises at times, so don't worry.

07:36.580 --> 07:40.540
Uh, Happy Valentine's.

07:40.540 --> 07:41.400
Thanks.

07:41.400 --> 07:43.570
Okay, here I go.

07:47.200 --> 07:49.990
Yeah, I like this.

07:52.790 --> 07:53.740
Thanks.

08:00.250 --> 08:04.670
It's a lot better now, but it still 
leaves a bad taste in my mouth.

08:04.670 --> 08:07.220
I'll have to practice 
before the next time.

08:07.220 --> 08:10.220
Maki-kun, you'll have 
dinner with us, won't you?

08:10.480 --> 08:12.380
Is there anything you'd like to eat?

08:12.380 --> 08:13.910
Oh, not really...

08:16.060 --> 08:16.850
Sora-san,

08:17.240 --> 08:20.240
is it okay if we use 
the kitchen for a bit?

08:20.930 --> 08:21.610
Sure.

08:22.030 --> 08:24.870
What are you making? 
Anything I can help out with?

08:24.870 --> 08:27.610
Thanks, but I'd like for us 
to do this by ourselves.

08:27.610 --> 08:30.720
Pick up where Umi left off, that is.

08:30.720 --> 08:31.870
You mean...

08:32.620 --> 08:35.480
I know I'm asking for a lot,

08:35.480 --> 08:39.290
but I want you try making 
chocolate for me one more time.

08:39.290 --> 08:44.220
I want to taste what your chocolate's like
when you don't have to compromise.

08:44.220 --> 08:47.360
When it's something 
you can present to me proudly.

08:48.270 --> 08:52.140
If you say so, I'm up for it.

08:52.450 --> 08:55.220
But it might turn out even worse 
than the last one, you know?

08:55.890 --> 08:59.810
Whatever you make, I'll eat it like 
it's the yummiest thing in the world.

09:00.130 --> 09:01.910
So be a tryhard, Umi.

09:01.910 --> 09:03.020
Dearie me.

09:03.020 --> 09:06.480
Look at Maki-kun, 
acting the passionate coach.

09:06.480 --> 09:08.190
You heard the boy.

09:08.190 --> 09:09.910
What will you do?

09:12.290 --> 09:15.450
Do you even have to ask?

09:15.450 --> 09:16.790
All right!

09:16.790 --> 09:18.040
If you so insist,

09:18.560 --> 09:22.670
I'm gonna use the rest of the ingredients 
to make a super-size chocolate.

09:22.970 --> 09:26.500
You'd better keep your word 
and accept it and my feelings.

09:26.500 --> 09:28.420
I will, thanks.

09:28.420 --> 09:30.220
Proud of you, girlfriend.

09:30.220 --> 09:34.920
And I don't know what I'm 
gonna do with you, boyfriend.

09:55.530 --> 09:57.810
Well? Is it good?

09:57.810 --> 10:01.230
Yeah, this is great. 
It's the flavor I just love.

10:02.200 --> 10:03.540
Thanks.

10:03.540 --> 10:07.630
It's a bit behind schedule, 
but I've managed to keep my word.

10:07.630 --> 10:08.610
Right?

10:08.610 --> 10:12.290
Right. I got a real taste 
of how you feel about me.

10:14.370 --> 10:17.930
I'm glad I didn't throw in the towel.

10:19.490 --> 10:21.180
Once Valentine's Day was past,

10:21.180 --> 10:25.210
its counterpart, White Day, 
arrived in a flash.

10:26.890 --> 10:31.750
Mm! It's not as sweet as I expected, 
but it's yummy all the same!

10:32.250 --> 10:37.670
It feels lighter than store-bought 
cookies. Like I can eat a whole bunch.

10:37.670 --> 10:41.160
Rep, you trying to be 
a househusband in the future?

10:41.160 --> 10:44.260
I'm not "trying" or anything...

10:45.190 --> 10:49.190
I-I wouldn't mind either way, 
if that's what you want.

10:49.190 --> 10:53.840
Heck, I would love the chance 
to look after you and stuff...

10:53.840 --> 10:59.700
Uh, I was just wondering if you were 
going to look at my gift or what.

10:59.700 --> 11:00.530
Huh?

11:00.930 --> 11:02.420
Oho?

11:02.420 --> 11:06.340
Where exactly did you think this 
conversation was going, my girl?

11:06.340 --> 11:08.130
I'm throwing hands! At Nina!

11:08.130 --> 11:10.650
Why me? What did I do to deserve this?!

11:11.070 --> 11:14.720
Why don't you just check your gift?

11:14.720 --> 11:19.400
You're his girlfriend. You might've 
gotten something different from us.

11:24.950 --> 11:27.000
When I looked into it,

11:27.430 --> 11:31.590
I found that different White Day gifts 
have different meanings attached to them.

11:31.960 --> 11:35.170
Cookies mean 
"Let's be friends for a long time."

11:35.450 --> 11:37.920
What does candy stand for, then?

11:39.590 --> 11:40.760
Er...

11:44.690 --> 11:46.480
It means "I love you."

11:48.020 --> 11:51.880
Yep, didn't have to hear that one 
to know what he said.

11:51.880 --> 11:54.280
Umi's so obvious.

11:54.940 --> 11:56.750
Maki, you jerk.

11:58.590 --> 12:00.160
Hey, Maki?

12:00.160 --> 12:00.840
Hmm?

12:01.650 --> 12:04.410
Is my present in your bag?

12:04.410 --> 12:07.660
Yeah. You'll see when we get there.

12:08.040 --> 12:10.790
I can't wait, but I'll be patient.

12:11.390 --> 12:16.440
Today is April 3rd: 
Umi's 17th birthday.

12:17.630 --> 12:19.470
Say, Umi.

12:19.470 --> 12:20.220
Hmm?

12:20.650 --> 12:23.930
Amami-san's house is pretty grand, huh?

12:23.930 --> 12:25.310
You think?

12:25.310 --> 12:29.390
Sure, it's twice as big as mine, but I'd 
say it still qualifies as a normal house.

12:29.780 --> 12:35.280
It seems that Umi's birthday celebrations 
happen at Amami-san's place every year.

12:36.250 --> 12:38.870
Welcome, you two!

12:41.550 --> 12:43.660
Hello, Auntie Eri.

12:43.920 --> 12:46.430
Happy birthday!

12:46.430 --> 12:50.590
I've made lots of food for you today, 
so feel free to eat your fill.

12:50.590 --> 12:51.370
I will.

12:51.660 --> 12:56.410
I don't know how to thank you 
for letting me use your place every year.

12:56.410 --> 13:01.110
It's fine. You're like 
a daughter to me, too.

13:01.110 --> 13:03.010
Is this the boy I've heard so much about?

13:03.710 --> 13:05.510
I'm Maehara Maki.

13:06.070 --> 13:09.270
Hello there. I'm Amami Eri.

13:11.220 --> 13:17.090
Lately, your name keeps coming up 
every time Yuu tells me about Umi-chan,

13:17.090 --> 13:23.570
so I've been wanting to meet the guy who 
made Yuu finally take an interest in boys.

13:23.570 --> 13:27.830
S-Stop that, Mom! 
I asked you not to bring that up!

13:27.830 --> 13:29.720
What's the big deal?

13:29.720 --> 13:33.340
He seems to be a very nice, 
gentle kid, just like you said.

13:36.590 --> 13:38.710
Happy birthday!

13:40.440 --> 13:43.010
Happy birthday, Umi!

13:43.550 --> 13:46.220
I'm so glad I could celebrate it 
with you again this year!

13:47.620 --> 13:49.310
Yeah, me too.

13:49.310 --> 13:51.180
I'm so happy.

13:53.090 --> 13:55.260
What were we thinking?

13:55.260 --> 13:59.230
Those two have always been 
special to each other.

14:06.300 --> 14:09.750
Dunno what's going on, but I want in!

14:11.470 --> 14:14.740
Don't all jump on me at once.

14:14.740 --> 14:16.540
You girls...

14:16.540 --> 14:21.800
All right, everyone. Help me bring 
the food and drinks to the table.

14:17.170 --> 14:19.800
We're like a can of sardines!

14:21.800 --> 14:23.510
Yes, ma'am!

14:36.200 --> 14:37.440
Okay, Umi.

14:37.440 --> 14:38.580
This one's from me.

14:39.140 --> 14:39.900
Yeah.

14:39.900 --> 14:40.970
Here we go.

14:40.970 --> 14:42.900
Today's main dish.

14:42.900 --> 14:44.110
Lucky her.

14:44.500 --> 14:48.120
Why are you all keeping your distance?

14:48.120 --> 14:49.650
I mean, you know...

14:49.650 --> 14:52.980
We figured we'd just get in your way.

14:52.980 --> 14:57.800
You might get distracted 
if you can see us.

14:57.800 --> 14:59.300
Right, Mom?

14:59.300 --> 15:01.500
Are they really that PDA?

15:01.500 --> 15:05.140
Yep. They really get into their 
own little lovey-dovey world.

15:05.140 --> 15:09.650
I'm just handing over my present 
like the rest of you did...

15:11.220 --> 15:13.760
What's so funny, Umi?

15:13.760 --> 15:16.230
Oh, no, nothing.

15:16.230 --> 15:18.270
Okay, here I go.

15:18.270 --> 15:19.040
Right.

15:20.590 --> 15:23.610
This is my birthday present to you.

15:24.510 --> 15:27.820
Er, happy birthday, Umi.

15:29.770 --> 15:31.830
Can I open it now?

15:32.170 --> 15:33.200
Sure.

15:40.340 --> 15:41.840
TO UMI, THANK YOU ALWAYS

15:42.420 --> 15:44.380
TO UMI, THANK YOU ALWAYS

15:45.150 --> 15:45.980
Silly.

15:50.270 --> 15:52.010
It's beautiful.

15:52.010 --> 15:54.980
I love the blue gradient.

15:55.250 --> 15:57.050
Is this a hairpin?

15:57.050 --> 16:01.580
Yeah. It goes well with 
party dresses and the like,

16:01.580 --> 16:03.190
or so the store assistant said.

16:04.110 --> 16:07.780
At first, I was going to get her 
something for daily use.

16:07.780 --> 16:10.500
But I ended up picking 
the opposite of that—

16:10.500 --> 16:13.760
something she might only use 
once a year if that, because...

16:14.630 --> 16:20.400
I pictured you wearing it and thought 
you'd look really beautiful.

16:21.710 --> 16:23.150
Ah...

16:23.790 --> 16:26.760
Do you mind if I put it on now?

16:27.380 --> 16:28.220
Go ahead.

16:32.260 --> 16:34.890
So, how do I look?

16:35.580 --> 16:38.600
Yeah, I was right on the money.

16:41.110 --> 16:43.570
You're beautiful, Umi.

16:46.300 --> 16:47.280
Thanks.

16:47.920 --> 16:50.590
I'll cherish this always.

16:50.590 --> 16:51.530
Sure.

16:53.820 --> 16:55.240
Say, Mom.

16:55.840 --> 16:56.910
What?

16:56.910 --> 17:00.420
Do you think I can find someone too?

17:01.160 --> 17:07.800
A boy who can bring out sides of me 
I never knew existed, like with Umi?

17:08.430 --> 17:11.090
Isn't that obvious?

17:11.510 --> 17:16.060
You were a labor of lots of love 
for your father and me.

17:16.410 --> 17:18.000
Love will always be in your life.

17:18.450 --> 17:19.860
Yeah?

17:21.340 --> 17:22.770
I believe you.

17:23.160 --> 17:27.230
I wonder who I'll come to 
fall in love with someday.

17:27.730 --> 17:29.800
I just hope they're nice.

17:31.210 --> 17:34.350
Filled with fantasies of 
a yet-unseen first love,

17:34.350 --> 17:39.790
a new season was about to roll 
into my—Amami Yuu's—life.

17:43.000 --> 17:45.340
Is this the detour you wanted to take?

17:45.340 --> 17:46.130
Yeah.

17:46.780 --> 17:51.590
Good. It's starting to shed, 
but half of it's still in bloom.

17:52.080 --> 17:56.300
Last spring, I just gazed at it 
from my apartment window,

17:56.300 --> 17:59.050
so I wanted to get 
a better look this time.

17:59.050 --> 18:00.730
Yeah, this is pretty.

18:01.300 --> 18:06.530
And I didn't want to go 
straight home either,

18:06.990 --> 18:08.360
but why here?

18:08.850 --> 18:11.210
No special reason.

18:11.800 --> 18:19.450
But it seemed like the perfect spot 
to express my thanks to you.

18:21.080 --> 18:22.420
Let's take a seat, yeah?

18:22.420 --> 18:23.160
Okay...

18:29.420 --> 18:33.840
You see, I never really 
liked the springtime.

18:34.620 --> 18:36.300
Really?

18:36.570 --> 18:40.470
Because you had to introduce 
yourself to the class every year?

18:40.740 --> 18:43.330
Embarrassing as it is to admit, yeah.

18:43.830 --> 18:46.560
Nobody was coming into 
or going out of my life,

18:46.560 --> 18:49.940
so it felt like all I was doing was 
embarrassing myself for no reason.

18:50.240 --> 18:55.720
Nice to meet you. I'm Maehara Maki.

18:50.750 --> 18:55.320
Overall, it was the time of year 
I felt most depressed.

18:57.430 --> 19:01.690
But I'm actually looking 
forward to it this year.

19:02.670 --> 19:04.500
Is that because...

19:05.120 --> 19:08.080
you have me?

19:08.390 --> 19:09.790
Of course.

19:09.790 --> 19:13.070
There's no guarantee we'll be in 
the same class for our second year,

19:13.070 --> 19:16.700
and I might be split up 
from the rest of the gang, too.

19:17.970 --> 19:21.720
But still, unlike before, 
I won't feel truly alone.

19:22.130 --> 19:24.930
I have friends who'll be there 
for me when I need them,

19:24.930 --> 19:29.380
and I have a girlfriend who'll 
stand by me when I feel lonely.

19:30.750 --> 19:35.090
Umi, thank you for being my friend,

19:35.830 --> 19:37.620
falling in love with me,

19:38.820 --> 19:41.720
and becoming my girlfriend.

19:43.580 --> 19:48.540
It's thanks to you that I'm taking small 
steps toward becoming a better guy.

19:48.990 --> 19:53.760
So please tell me whenever you're 
the least bit worried about something.

19:54.120 --> 19:56.080
You don't have to hold anything back.

19:56.080 --> 20:01.520
Are you sure? You won't get sick of me 
when I start telling you everything?

20:02.030 --> 20:06.760
Even I get surprised by how clingy 
and needy I can be sometimes, y'know?

20:07.100 --> 20:11.060
I get jealous over everything, 
and I'm desperate for attention...

20:11.750 --> 20:17.780
I'm sure. That just proves 
how much you love me.

20:20.500 --> 20:24.520
You're mine, and that's the bottom line.

20:25.710 --> 20:27.080
Your gentle, kind nature,

20:27.080 --> 20:28.870
and even how you're kind of a wimp...

20:29.240 --> 20:32.590
Every bit of you belongs 
to me, and me alone.

20:33.030 --> 20:34.050
Yeah.

20:34.050 --> 20:37.600
I'm yours always, Umi.

20:47.690 --> 20:49.560
Yeah, I knew it.

20:56.030 --> 20:58.100
You finally realized?

20:58.100 --> 21:01.380
Have I grown a little taller?

21:01.380 --> 21:02.280
Bingo.

21:06.050 --> 21:08.290
Excuse me for one second.

21:16.860 --> 21:22.300
You may be a bit taller now, but 
you're still a ways off my ideal height.

21:23.250 --> 21:24.760
What do you mean?

21:24.760 --> 21:30.450
As much as I like how we can look 
each other straight in the eye right now,

21:31.360 --> 21:37.480
I'd also enjoy a height gap where I'd have
to get on my tippy-toes to kiss you.

21:39.560 --> 21:42.950
Yeah, I don't think 
I'm going to grow that tall.

21:44.340 --> 21:48.220
But I'll do my best to become 
your ideal man in every way I can.

21:49.230 --> 21:51.840
Yeah, you do that, Maki!

21:55.170 --> 21:58.500
With my new goal made somewhat clear,

21:59.070 --> 22:03.770
we took our first steps to a new season.

